  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#14351\", \"PowerToys#3610\", \"PowerToys#23\"], \"answer\": \"This feature has been requested before. It is usually called Quick Switch, after Listary's version. It lets you jump an Open/Save dialog to the folder of an open Explorer window. PowerToys#14351 is the main tracking issue, and the maintainers closed similar requests as duplicates of it. PowerToys#3610 and PowerToys#23 describe the same idea. The archive shows no sign that it has been built, so you can't get it in PowerToys yet. Add your +1 or your Dialog Jump use case (the Ctrl+G hotkey, the folder search box, Lertaro and Flow Launcher as open-source references) to #14351. Until then, you can use Listary, Lertaro, Flow Launcher's Dialog Jump or Fluent Search. Fluent Search was mentioned in #23 as supporting this.\"}",
